# Assets the game loads

The game loads everything below by relative URL from the delivery root, so
the artist's `assets/` directory must sit next to `index.html` (it is the
artist's delivered path; this repository does not contain it). The loader is
`js/assets.js` (sprites, sounds) plus two `<img>` tags in `index.html`. A
missing file logs a warning and the game draws a plain shape in the palette
instead, so the build never breaks on art; the delivered game is expected to
have every file. Names follow the artist's manifest, `assets/README.md`.

## Board

- Playing field: 20 columns x 20 rows, cell size **32 px**, surrounded by one
  ring of wall cells; canvas 704 x 704 px (22 x 22 cells), scaled by CSS to
  fit the window with pixelated scaling.
- Score / best HUD is HTML text above the board; title, pause and game-over
  screens are HTML overlays over the board.

## Images

| File | Size | How the game uses it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `assets/img/snake_head.png` | 32 x 32 | Head, faces right; rotated in 90 deg steps to the heading. |
| `assets/img/snake_body.png` | 32 x 32 | Even body segments (not rotated). |
| `assets/img/snake_body_alt.png` | 32 x 32 | Odd body segments, for stripes (not rotated). |
| `assets/img/food.png` | 32 x 32 | Food. |
| `assets/img/tile.png` | 32 x 32 | Every playing-field cell. |
| `assets/img/wall.png` | 32 x 32 | The ring of wall cells around the field. |
| `assets/img/logo.png` | 320 x 120 | Title screen; replaces the text heading "SNAKE". |
| `assets/img/gameover.png` | 400 x 120 | Game-over screen; replaces the text heading. Cause, final score and Play again stay as text below. |

## Sounds (WAV)

| File | Played when |
| --- | --- |
| `assets/audio/start.wav` | a game starts (Start / Play again) |
| `assets/audio/eat.wav` | the snake eats food |
| `assets/audio/turn.wav` | an arrow key changes the heading |
| `assets/audio/gameover.wav` | the snake hits a wall or itself |

## Palette

`css/style.css` takes its colours from the manifest's palette (`--bg`,
`--grid`, `--wall`, `--text`, `--accent`, `--food`, ...). If the palette
changes, tell game-developer or ship an `assets/theme.css` overriding those
custom properties and ask for it to be linked.
